IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`
IMPORT `P4-art-36`

-- Tests of Article 36 (consolidated lines 599-621). Expected values are written from the text.
-- Each gated function: a case before (1 August 2025), on (2 August 2025) and after the date Chapter III Section 4 applies.
-- Each period: a case on each side of its end.

§ `Article 36(1) and (2)`

-- args: date asked, a relevant change, the authority notified the Commission and the other Member States, via the electronic notification tool
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` (Date 1 12 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(1) the duty of the notifying authority to notify the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notifying authority` DOES `Art 36(1) notify the Commission and the other Member States of the relevant change via the electronic notification tool` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 36(1) the duty of the notifying authority to notify the relevant change` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- args: date asked, the change is an extension of the scope, the change is another change
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the procedures that apply to the change to the notification` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Art 36(2) the procedures of Articles 29 and 30`
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the procedures that apply to the change to the notification` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `Art 36(2) the procedures of paragraphs (3) to (9) of Article 36`
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the procedures that apply to the change to the notification` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the procedures that apply to the change to the notification` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 36(3): the notice of cessation, one year before a planned cessation`

-- args: date asked, decided to cease, the cessation is planned, has informed the authority and the providers, the date it informed them, the date it ceases
-- Planned cessation on 1 January 2027: one year before is 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not planned: "as soon as possible" gives no period.
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rule: decided on 2 September 2025, ceasing on 2 September 2027: the deadline is 2 September 2026, 365 days after the decision.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority and the providers of a planned cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 2 9 2025) (Date 2 9 2027) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notified body` DOES `Art 36(3) inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned of the planned cessation` AT 365
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority and the providers of a planned cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 2 9 2025) (Date 2 9 2027) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notified body` DOES `Art 36(3) inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned of the planned cessation` AT 366
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority and the providers of a planned cessation` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 2 9 2025) (Date 2 9 2027) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 366
-- Not yet applicable: no breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority and the providers of a planned cessation` (Date 1 8 2025) (Date 2 9 2025) (Date 2 9 2027) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§ `Article 36(3): nine months of validity, and the full assessment`

-- args: date asked, the date the body ceased, another notified body has confirmed in writing. Ceased on 1 October 2025: nine months end on 1 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 2 7 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 30 9 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` (Date 1 8 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the date the former body ceased, the date the latter body completed the full assessment, the latter body has issued new certificates, the date it first issued them
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 2 7 2026) TRUE (Date 5 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 2 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` (Date 1 8 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the body has ceased its activity, the authority has withdrawn the designation
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) fourth sentence the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation of a notified body that has ceased` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) fourth sentence the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation of a notified body that has ceased` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) fourth sentence the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation of a notified body that has ceased` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(3) fourth sentence the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation of a notified body that has ceased` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notifying authority to withdraw the designation` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notifying authority` DOES `Art 36(3) withdraw the designation of the notified body that has ceased its activity` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 36(3) the duty of the notifying authority to withdraw the designation` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

