§ `Article 36(5): telling the providers within 10 days`

-- args: date asked, the designation has been suspended, restricted or withdrawn, the date of it, the body has informed the providers, the date it informed them
-- Suspended on 1 September 2025: the tenth day is 11 September 2025.
#ASSERT `Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE (Date 1 9 2025) TRUE (Date 11 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE (Date 1 9 2025) TRUE (Date 12 9 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE (Date 1 9 2025) FALSE (Date 11 9 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE (Date 1 9 2025) FALSE (Date 11 9 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE (Date 1 9 2025) TRUE (Date 11 9 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rule: day 0 is the day of the suspension; the breach path is a notice on day 11, or none by day 11.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(5) the duty of the notified body to inform the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notified body` DOES `Art 36(5) inform the providers concerned` AT 10
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 36(5) the duty of the notified body to inform the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 36 notified body` DOES `Art 36(5) inform the providers concerned` AT 11
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 36(5) the duty of the notified body to inform the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 11
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 36(5) the duty of the notified body to inform the providers concerned within 10 days` (Date 1 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

