§ `Article 36(8)`

-- (a): args: the date of the suspension or restriction, the authority confirmed there is no risk, the date of the confirmation, the authority outlined a timeline.
-- Suspended on 1 March 2026: "within one month" ends on 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Suspended on 31 January 2026: one month later is 28 February 2026 (the last day of the month).
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b): args: the date of the suspension or restriction, confirmed no certificates will be issued, states the capability, determined the body is not capable, the provider confirmed in writing, the date of the provider's confirmation
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS FALSE
-- The list: args: date asked, the certificate was unduly issued, the designation has been suspended or restricted, circumstance (a) holds, circumstance (b) holds
#ASSERT `Art 36(8) the certificates remain valid after a suspension or restriction` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
